Feature: Residual Python effect surfaces fail closed
  The TypeScript CStar kernel owns lifecycle records and durable estate state.
  Detached Python calculation and lexical helpers grant no authority.

  Scenario: Validation persistence uses the kernel result surface
    When a caller invokes the former Python validation save helper
    Then it returns legacy_python_validation_persistence_retired_use_cstar_record_result
    And no Hall or filesystem mutation begins

  Scenario: Autonomous watchers and sandbox execution are retired
    When a caller constructs the former stability watcher or runs the sandbox warden
    Then the action returns its stable retirement error
    And no filesystem watcher Docker subprocess or network action begins

  Scenario: Python memory remains detached
    When a caller uses the Python memory compatibility index
    Then its records remain process local and non-authoritative
    And Chroma and Hall are never opened
    And the former Hall escape hatch returns legacy_python_memory_authority_retired_use_cstar_kernel

  Scenario: Pure calculation remains available
    When a caller runs the detached SPRT calculus
    Then it returns a result from the supplied trials only
    And it records no validation result or lifecycle transition
